# RR2c-3 (critical_qualifier_receivers_bug; steps/qualifier-receivers-20261010.md; the author's example of 2026-10-10,
# LMX_blog/2026-10-10.md#qualifier-receivers-20261010, as written): a merge in a method's `return:`, under the chain
# `independent: const: immutable:` or bare, is the method's result -- the merge declares a hidden row the method
# returns; its typed operand reads the formal; the caller receives the Structure through a reference binding and
# reads its field.  Under --walk-methods the methods stay native (the walk's return of the row is RR2d's).  Exit 7;
# 81..83 name the failing call.
Integer:
    int: value 0
end: Integer
fn: getInteger (int: newValue) Integer
    return: independent: const: immutable: merge(Integer  int: value newValue)
end: getInteger
fn: plainInteger (int: newValue) Integer
    return: merge(Integer  int: value newValue)
end: plainInteger
fn: ownInteger (int: newValue) Integer
    return: independent: merge(Integer; (int: value newValue))
end: ownInteger
fn: m () int
    @: Integer got getInteger(7)
    if: got\value != 7
        return: 81
    @: Integer plain plainInteger(5)
    if: plain\value != 5
        return: 82
    @: Integer own ownInteger(3)
    if: own\value != 3
        return: 83
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
